  "objective_summary": "Landed SemanticReconciliation@1 as the accelerator merge composition surface that gates merge admission and refreshes canonical semantic state after queue acceptance without becoming a second semantic truth authority. Before merge the surface verifies predicted effects, contracts, selected tests/proofs, governor findings, available assurance, and an incremental seal. After queue acceptance it records a datasets-authority canonical tree scan, compares predicted vs observed deltas, invalidates dependents, updates the world snapshot identity, reevaluates goals, and revises until settled. MergeQueue now exposes verify_pre_merge_admission and complete_with_semantic_reconciliation so the queue cannot mark a request completed until both pre-merge admission and post-acceptance settlement pass. Soft-mode rejections leave the claim processing for retry. Workers cannot publish canonical roots; worker completion or task status alone never authorizes acceptance.",
